# TalkStay design sync

## Canonical sources
- **Marketing (mobile + desktop):** `src/talkstay/pages/Landing.tsx` on latest `main` — one responsive hero, not separate mobile/desktop pages.
- **Demo hub art/CTAs:** `src/talkstay/pages/DemoHub.tsx` + `public/marketing/role-*` (labels under images; no text baked into art).
- **Guest phone UI:** keep `GuestApp.tsx` and `DemoGuestApp.tsx` shells aligned when changing chrome.
- **Staff shell:** keep `HotelApp.tsx` and `DemoApp.tsx` aligned when changing nav/sidebar.
- **Guest access wording:** use `src/talkstay/lib/guestAccessCopy.ts` — do not invent parallel QR-only copy.

## Always
- Branch from **latest `main`**. Do not continue superseded hero branches (`hero-message-journey-*`, `manager-guest-demo-images-*`) — those regress the current design.
- Ignore unused TalkWeb leftovers (`src/pages/Index.tsx`, `src/components/HeroSection.tsx`) — they are not routed.
- After landing copy/layout changes, check DemoHub + meta in `index.html` so mobile home-screen / social previews match.

## Hero intent (current)
Voice-first badge · guest-in-bed promo · “Handled *beautifully.* / from anywhere” · value line with Ask/Request journey · image-first on mobile · role graphics without overlays.
